commit 39682669cc8a582406fe4a6c0d0214b15291db42
Author: Marcus Schack Abildskov <work@marcus-sa.dev>
Date:   Sun Nov 22 16:17:27 2026 +0100

    build(cloud-hypervisor): pin the fork that exits 111 when a volume disk is held
    
    The fork exits 111 when a disk's exclusive open fails with EBUSY (ADR-0319), so the
    driver can report a held volume as a typed failure. Pin the fork revision and the
    metal checksum, record the exit status as a wire contract, and keep the metal probe
    that shows 111 for a held device, 1 for a missing disk, and a normal open for a free one.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

