Date:   Sun Nov 22 15:10:09 2026 +0100

    main: exit 111 when a disk's exclusive open fails with EBUSY
    
    A raw disk is opened with O_EXCL; when another holder has the device the open
    fails with EBUSY, which exited 1 like every other start failure. Walk the error
    chain for the typed BlockError (kind Io, op Open, source io::Error EBUSY) and
    exit 111 for exactly that case. Every other failure still exits 1.
    
    Signed-off-by: Marcus Schack Abildskov <work@marcus-sa.dev>

